The "automatic loading" entry point: get_candles(symbol, timeframe,
count) transparently checks the cache, downloads only what's missing,
optionally fills gaps, and returns — callers never manage cache vs.
download themselves.

- Incremental updates: _sync_recent compares the cache's latest candle
  to now and downloads only enough candles to bridge that gap
  (int(staleness / step) + 1), not a full re-fetch of count. Falls
  back to a full download only when nothing is cached yet.
- Gap filling: for each gap data.storage.find_gaps reports, requests
  just enough candles (span / step + 2, a small buffer) ending at the
  gap's far edge via get_candles' new end parameter, filters to what
  actually falls inside the gap window, and saves it.
- sync() combines incremental download + gap fill + validation into
  one call with a structured SyncReport, for a scheduled job.

Built against broker.base.BrokerGateway, not MT5 directly — this
milestone's brief described this module as an "MT5 history download",
but the Quant Core (which this is part of) must never import a broker
SDK directly, per the Broker Foundation milestone's own architecture.
A caller who wants MT5 history gets it by passing an MT5Gateway in;
nothing here hardcodes a broker. See docs/architecture.md.

9 tests covering empty-cache full download, incremental-update download
sizing, fresh-cache no-op, gap filling (and fill_gaps=False leaving a
gap unfilled on purpose), and sync()'s report.
